  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Lose it – win it back",
  "description": "Half a rink with a goalkeeper in goal. The centre line is the turning line. Play 4 v 4. The goalkeeper throws out to blue, who must get over the centre line with the ball or pass a team-mate over it. If they manage it, they turn and attack the goal while red defend.\n\nIf red win the ball they attack the goal straight away – and blue must react. The nearest blue skates at the ball carrier at once, the others close the passes and mark near the ball. If the ball cannot be won straight back, blue skate back goal-side and win it a little later. If the ball goes over the end line or the boards, the next attempt starts with a new throw-out.\n\nBigger version: 6 v 6, where blue have four seconds to win the ball back – otherwise the attempt stops. Let only one team work on the transition at first, then both. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The nearest player goes straight at the ball when it is lost."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The others close the passes around the ball and pick up the players near it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If you cannot win it straight back: skate back between the ball and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Decide together when to press and when to drop."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
